.TH SPP-DELETE-APP 1 "October 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
spp-delete-app \- Delete an SPP application context and all its data (files, config, caches, views)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php delete:app
\fIAppName\fR
[\fB\-\-config\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-backup\fR]
[\fB\-\-keep\-db\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B delete:app
removes an SPP application and its associated resources, caches, and configuration.
Supports \fB\-\-config\-only\fR mode to preserve source files in \fBsrc/\fR while unregistering
configurations and virtual hosts, and \fB\-\-backup\fR to generate an archive prior to deletion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I AppName
(Required) Name of the application to delete.
.TP
.BR \-\-config\-only
Only remove configuration, caches, and domain bindings; keep source code in \fBsrc/\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-backup
Create a full zip backup archive in \fBvar/backups/apps/\fR before deleting.
.TP
.BR \-\-force
Skip confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-keep\-db
Preserve database tables (only remove files and config).
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be deleted without actually deleting anything.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spp-app-uninstall (1),
.BR spp-app-backup (1),
.BR spp-app-restore (1)
